32-bit build fix (25.09): MdpReplayEngine::Replay's three pointer->cmdqU32Ptr_t
conversions (submit.metas, submit.prop_addr, submit.hw_metas_read_v1) went
through reinterpret_cast<cmdqU32Ptr_t>(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(ptr)). On
a 32-bit build uintptr_t is unsigned int while cmdqU32Ptr_t is unsigned long
long (the CMDQ ioctl ABI's pointer field is always 64-bit; a 32-bit caller
zero-extends into it), so that inner-to-outer step is a widening integer
conversion, which reinterpret_cast does not allow: "reinterpret_cast from
'uintptr_t' (aka 'unsigned int') to 'cmdqU32Ptr_t' (aka 'unsigned long
long') is not allowed" at MdpReplay.cpp:240, :244 and :249. Changed the
outer cast to static_cast<cmdqU32Ptr_t>(...), an ordinary integer
conversion; the inner pointer-to-uintptr_t reinterpret_cast is unchanged.
Not built on a device in either width; to verify: MdpReplay.cpp compiles
with zero warnings under both the 64-bit toolchain this patch was already
checked against and a 32-bit (arm) one.

